1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,660
Hello English learners and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:07,640
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:08,640
I'm Amira.

4
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:14,260
And Amira and I are here today with a great, great lesson for you.

5
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:15,280
Yes, we are.

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,220
Today we're going to be talking about a restaurant.

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,980
Amira, why don't you give us a little bit more details?

8
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:29,000
Well, we're talking about a situation in a restaurant and two people are involved, the waiter and the customer.

9
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:30,870
And I don't want to say any more.

10
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,330
Okay, don't say any more.

11
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:37,610
Let's just listen to this dialogue and we'll be back later to explain it.

12
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:45,100
Good evening.

13
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,500
My name is Fabio.

14
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:47,800
I'll be your waiter for tonight.

15
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:49,000
May I take your order?

16
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:51,510
No, I'm still working on it.

17
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:53,090
This menu is not even in English.

18
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:54,630
What's good here?

19
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,740
For you, sir, I would recommend spaghetti and meatballs.

20
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:02,120
Does it come with coke and fries?

21
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:09,120
It comes with either soup or salad and a complimentary glass of wine, sir.

22
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:14,790
I'll go with the spaghetti and meatballs, salad and the wine.

23
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:16,650
Excellent choice.

24
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:19,470
Your order will be ready soon.

25
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:21,350
How soon is soon?

26
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,480
Twenty minutes.

27
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:24,770
You know what?

28
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,770
I'll go grab a burger across the street.

29
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:30,160
What a waiter!

30
00:01:35,710 --> 00:01:36,270
What a waiter!

31
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:42,630
He is really angry at this customer and I can't blame him.

32
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:43,950
I would be angry too.

33
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:45,760
Yeah.

34
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:50,750
So, I think, Marco, you have chosen some interesting expressions for us here.

35
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,170
What is the first one?

36
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:56,250
Well, the first one is I'm still working on it.

37
00:01:56,490 --> 00:01:58,150
I'm still working on it.

38
00:01:58,390 --> 00:02:00,410
I'm still working on it.

39
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:02,420
I'm still working on it.

40
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:09,200
Why don't we listen to some other examples on how you can use this word and then we'll come back and explain it.

41
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,880
Did you finish reading the magazine?

42
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,740
I'm still working on it.

43
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,540
Did you fix my car?

44
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:28,800
I'm still working on it.

45
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:40,000
Ah, so you could say I'm still working on it means I still need more time.

46
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:40,150
Fantastic.

47
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Great.

48
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
OK, it's clear.

49
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,330
I have another one for you guys.

50
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:48,030
It's a phrase commonly used and you'll hear it all the time.

51
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,410
Coke and fries.

52
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:50,710
Coke and fries.

53
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,230
Coke and fries.

54
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:53,430
Coke and fries.

55
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,690
It's a short way of saying Coca-Cola and French fries.

56
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,230
So that's basically America's fast food.

57
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,660
Yeah, burger, coke and fries.

58
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,520
OK.

59
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,440
